{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "oan-da-visits",
    "name": "OAN DA Visits",
    "description": "Plan / list / reschedule / cancel / start / submit farm visits with a farmer.\n\nBase path: /api/v1/da-services\n\n## Run order (happy path)\n1. SSO Login — `POST /api/v1/da-services/sso/login` with `username`, `password`, `key`. Set `user` to the DA's Frappe User (email), usually the same as `usr` when a DA self-plans\n2. (Optional) GET farmer profile — confirms farmer exists in DA Farmer Reference / registry cache\n3. (Optional, Manual kebele mode only) Create farmer link — Supervisor\n4. Plan a visit (requires `user`) → stores visit_id\n4b. (Optional) Plan visits batch — body `{ user, visits: [1..5] }` same route\n5. Get visit / List visits\n6. Start visit → Submit outcome → (optional) Attachments\n7. Activity report\n\n## Auth\nSign in with SSO Login only (`POST /api/v1/da-services/sso/login`). Visits are DA Services native DocTypes — send `Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}`. No staff CSRF pair is required for these routes (unlike Crop / Livestock / Grievance registry intake); `csrf_token` is stored from SSO for other collections that need it.\n\n## Scope\nAccess and row visibility: DA Visit DocType permissions + permission hooks + User Permissions (`get_list` / `check_permission` / create). No hardcoded `require_roles` on visit handlers. List query args only narrow the permitted set (date, status, farmer_id, da_id, region, zone, woreda, kebele).\n\n## Farmer registry before link / schedule\n- **Manual farmer link** (`POST /farmer-links`): farmer must already exist in **DA Farmer Reference** (synced from Farmer Registry), `registration_state=APPROVED`, same Kebele as the DA's Effective Manual assignment. It does **not** call the live Farmer Registry API at link time.\n- **Plan visit** (`POST /visits`): requires `farmer_id`, `user` (User Link for the assigned DA), and `scheduled_at` (or date+time). Does **not** verify the farmer against Farmer Registry or require an active DA Farmer Link. Does **not** fall back to session user when `user` is omitted. Specialization conflict on open visits for the same farmer is checked.\n\nDatetimes are site-local (Africa/Addis_Ababa in prod), ISO without offset.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
